{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\n// Defined in habeas_sdk::graph.\n#[derive(serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize)]\npub struct Record<N, L = ()> {\n    /// Application-chosen revision of this criterion's review rules.\n    pub revision: String,\n    /// Observations captured by the SDK.\n    pub dependencies: Vec<Dependency<N, L>>,\n    /// Serialized Criterion::Ok; interpretation belongs to the application.\n    pub output: serde_json::Value,\n}\n```\n\nThe SDK constructs the dependencies from execution's trace and encodes the\ncompleted result using its Serde JSON representation; there is no required\nboolean, rationale, or metadata shape. `Record`, `Dependency`, and\n`Fingerprint` support Serde when their type parameters do. The graph's node\nidentities and edge labels need not implement Serde unless its storage backend\nrequires those bounds.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The three `{test}` items cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record`.\n\n- **Output encoding.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_have_independent_typed_answers_and_cache_negative_results]` checks that the stored `output` is the Serde JSON of the completed result. A custom `Answer` struct is stored as `{\"satisfied\": false, \"details\": [...]}`. A `Judgment` whose `metadata` disagrees with its `result` is stored as `serde_json::to_value(&judgment)`. A plain `Vec<String>` and a negative answer are also stored and read back. This shows the requirement's \"no required boolean, rationale, or metadata shape\": different result types are accepted and encoded unchanged. The same test checks that records for criteria with no reads have empty `dependencies`.\n- **Dependencies from the execution trace.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[changed_dependencies_precede_decoding_and_execution_records_its_own_reads]` checks that the stored record's dependencies equal `[Dependency::Node(Node(2), Fingerprint{scheme:\"text-v1\", value:\"after\"})]`. It also checks that the freshness check's read and the execution's own read are recorded separately (`reads == [2,2]`), so only the execution's trace is used.\n- **Serde support and the bounds.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs#fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` round-trips a `Record` through `FileEvidenceStorage`. It covers `revision`, `dependencies` and `output` for `Dependency::Node` with `String` nodes. It also covers `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` with a non-ASCII label and a `Fingerprint`. These are the only two `Dependency` variants. It also checks that a mismatched type parameter (`u8`) gives a JSON error.\n- **Node identities and edge labels need no Serde.** The `Node` type in `contracts.rs` and `agent.rs` deliberately lacks Serde. The in-memory graph domains use it with the `Validator`, and their tests execute and record evidence without Serde bounds.\n\nI found no uncovered MUST, SHOULD or boundary case. The `output` ordering and failure behaviour belongs to the refining `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output`, which has its own tests and is not assessed here.",
  "references": "1de4bc8cde8a0da55f204faddbeafbe2fbede33f90036ae53604885c8626a3d6",
